  "card": "Makes the default combined fee estimator in estimatesmartfee fall back to the block policy estimate whenever the mempool estimator cannot produce an estimate, rather than returning an error. It changes the mempool estimator to return an error instead of the minimum relay fee floor when the mempool is too sparse to fill block percentiles, preventing severe fee underestimation on nodes with empty or sparse mempools. In addition, when mempool loading fails at startup, the estimator clears its mined-block window to avoid serving estimates based on stale mempool state, and renames the combined estimator option in RPC from 'none' to 'auto'.",
